on-arrival: constitutional_restraint += 6; president_relation += 3; judicial_legitimacy += 2; tribunal_domestic_recognition += 3; ko_relation -= 2; pis_relation += 1; eu_relations += 3; news_headline = "The Left refuses both Polexit rhetoric and legal shortcuts"

= Constitutional credibility is defended and nobody thanks us for it

Our line is that a disputed court's ruling is a problem to be undone lawfully,
by repairing appointments and referring the question properly, and not by
declaring the judgment imaginary. It is the position a future government of
ours would need, and we take it while in opposition, when it costs.

The liberal wing hears equivocation and says so. PiS hears a party that will
not call the Tribunal a fiction and quotes us approvingly, which is worse.

