= October 2021 — Repealed for the wrong reason

The Commission has begun holding back regional programme money from councils
that adopted the declarations, and the Norwegian funds have done the same.
Within weeks, county after county votes to rescind — several of them with the
same councillors who voted them in, explaining that the resolution was
symbolic, that nothing was ever meant by it, and that the money is needed for a
road.

This is a victory and it is worth being precise about what kind. Nobody has
been persuaded. A price was attached, and the price was paid. The young people
who spent two years living in a county that had voted about them get a repeal
without an apology and without anything replacing it.

[? if zones_response = "Legal challenge": The administrative-court challenges
we funded in 2019 are producing their first judgments in the same months, which
means some of these councils are repealing one step ahead of a court.?]
[? if zones_response = "European conditionality": We asked Brussels to attach
this condition in 2019. It worked exactly as we said it would, and the
government has spent two years telling those counties whose idea it was.?]
[? if zones_response = "Local organising": Our organisers have been in these
counties since 2019, which is why in a handful of them the repeal is moved by
somebody local rather than by a treasurer with a spreadsheet.?]
[? if zones_response = "National confrontation": We made this a national
argument in 2019 and it stayed one, so the repeals are being reported as
Brussels defeating Poland rather than as councils changing their minds.?]
[? if zones_response = "": The Left never took a position on the resolutions,
so nobody is asking us what the repeals mean.?]

- @zones21_replace
- @zones21_claim
- @zones21_audit

