= March 2022 — Emergency welcome needs public services

Ukrainian families arrive at stations, private flats and hastily converted
halls. Volunteers carry the first weeks; municipal leaders—including Warsaw
mayor **[? if president_name = "Rafał Trzaskowski": Marcin Kierwiński?][? if
president_name != "Rafał Trzaskowski": Rafał Trzaskowski?]**—warn that
goodwill cannot create school places, clinic staff or long-term housing.
Teachers, nurses and social workers are already absorbing the emergency into
services strained before the invasion.

The lasting political question is whether the state will build capacity for
refugees and receiving communities together—or allow solidarity to depend on
who still has a spare room and enough energy to volunteer.

- @mar22_services
- @mar22_volunteers
- @mar22_equal
- @mar22_screen

