= May 2022 — The cost of one opposition list

[? if not may22_pis_list_route:
Rising mortgage payments intensify criticism of the government's economic
management. <span class="party-ko"><b>Donald Tusk</b></span>, KO chair and former prime minister, also asks every
opposition party to stand on a single electoral list under a common democratic
argument, forcing Lewica to weigh a cleaner anti-PiS contest against its own
programme, candidates and public subsidy.
?]

[? if may22_pis_list_route:
Rising mortgage payments intensify criticism of the government's economic
management, but our breach with KO has changed the electoral question. KO chair
Donald Tusk's one-list appeal now excludes a Lewica that bargained with, or
entered, Prime Minister Mateusz Morawiecki's governing camp. If that alignment
is to survive an election, PiS chair Jarosław Kaczyński must decide whether his
party list has room for our candidates—and we must decide what accepting his
control would cost.
?]

