Hospitals, schools and households below a clear income threshold receive the
first guarantee. The narrower package is cheaper and directs money toward the
people least able to absorb another bill.

Families just above the line become the opposition's counterexample, and Razem
warns that means testing can turn a universal energy crisis into another queue
for proof of poverty.

- @sep22_reparations: Turn to the reparations report


