@nov22_przewodow
title: Przewodów
new-page: true
view-if: przewodow_2022_done = 0 and independence_2022_done = 1
on-arrival: przewodow_2022_done = 1; war_escalation_risk += 10

= Two people are dead

It comes down on a grain-drying facility just outside **Przewodów**, six
kilometres from the Ukrainian border, at about half past three in the
afternoon. Two farm workers are killed. Russia has spent the day firing the
largest barrage of the war at Ukraine's power grid, and the first reports out
of the village say Russian missile.

By evening the picture is less certain. Western officials briefing anonymously
say the fragments look like a Ukrainian air-defence interceptor, fired at
incoming Russian missiles and fallen on the wrong side of the border.
President Zelensky says publicly that it was not Ukrainian. The Polish
government convenes the National Security Council and does not use the word
attack.

Article 4 consultations are being discussed in Brussels. NATO's readiness
depends on facts nobody has yet established, and the studios are already
booking guests who will supply certainty in the meantime.

Two people are dead in a village of four hundred, and the difference between
the available explanations is the difference between an accident of an air
defence protecting a city and the first Russian strike on alliance
territory.

- @nov22_verify
- @nov22_russia
- @nov22_ukraine_blame

@nov22_verify
title: Verify, consult NATO and communicate uncertainty
on-arrival: president_relation += 4; military_trust += 4; public_trust += 4; war_escalation_risk -= 12; constitutional_restraint += 2; news_headline = "Verification outruns escalation at Przewodów"

We say that two Polish citizens are dead, that the origin of the missile is
under investigation, and that we will not speculate about Article 4 until the
fragments have been examined. It is an unsatisfying thing to say on a night
when everyone wants a sentence.

It is also what allows the alliance to work. Consultation exists to establish
facts before commitments; a party that pre-empts it makes the procedure harder
to use next time. By morning the anonymous briefings have moved toward the
interceptor and our restraint looks like judgment rather than timidity.

- @nov22_return: Return to the November desk

@nov22_russia
title: Attribute political responsibility to Russia immediately
on-arrival: ukraine_solidarity += 3; military_trust += 1; public_trust -= 2; war_escalation_risk += 8; konf_poll_momentum += 0.1; news_headline = "The Left names Russia before the technical finding"

We say Russia is responsible, which is true in the sense that matters: nothing
falls on Przewodów in a year when Moscow is not firing at the grid sixty
kilometres away. The statement is popular, morally clear and lands before
anyone else's.

The technical finding is not obliged to agree with the political one. If the
fragments turn out to be Ukrainian, our sentence stays on camera and the
distinction we meant — responsibility for the war, not for the missile — will
be the part nobody replays.

- @nov22_return: Return to the November desk

@nov22_ukraine_blame
title: Demand Ukrainian culpability before alliance consultation
on-arrival: ukraine_solidarity -= 7; war_fatigue += 4; war_escalation_risk += 3; konf_poll_momentum += 0.4; anti_establishment_youth_konf_affinity += 2; news_headline = "Przewodów becomes an anti-Ukrainian wedge"

We demand that Kyiv answer for the deaths before NATO has finished looking at
the debris. It is the first time a Polish parliamentary party has pointed at
Ukraine over a Polish casualty, and it does not go unnoticed in either capital.

Konfederacja has been waiting a year for somebody respectable to cross that
line first. Our own Ukraine-solidarity organisers, who spent the spring driving
vans to the border, find out from the television what their party now thinks.

- @nov22_return: Return to the November desk

