= May 2023 — A verdict before the election

The PiS majority passes a law creating a state commission to investigate
Russian influence and gives it the power to condemn public figures without a
criminal trial.
Donald Tusk—the KO leader, former prime minister and obvious target—calls it a
court assembled for his removal. [? if president_name = "Andrzej Duda":
President Andrzej Duda says he will sign the law.?][? if president_name !=
"Andrzej Duda": President **[+ president_name +]** says the commission cannot
take effect in this form and promises a veto.?]

Tusk has already summoned the opposition to Warsaw on 4 June, the anniversary
of the 1989 election. What began as his demonstration can now become a defence
of the democratic field itself. Lewica must help fill the streets without
vanishing into the political biography of the man most likely to lead them.

- @may23_front
- @may23_legal
- @may23_contingent
- @may23_caution

