= 15 June 2023 — A challenger appears

At a small Warsaw press conference, party chair **Chrystian Szpilski**,
secretary-general **Patryk Spaliński** and co-founder **Maciej Kozłowski**
present <span class="party party-nowa-solidarnosc">**Nowa Solidarność**</span>.
Publicly backed by urban activist **Jan Śpiewak**,
the new party promises a patriotic, economically left alternative, an
independent run for the Sejm and Senate, and a direct challenge to the
parliamentary Left.

Three leaders, one banner and one week of online attention: at last, we have a
challenger.

- @jun23_nowa_solidarnosc_dissolves: See how its first week goes


@jun23_nowa_solidarnosc_dissolves
# prose-audit: Grade A — The follow-up turns the documented resignations and vanishing accounts into a factual one-week dissolution gag.
title: The challenger dissolves
new-page: true
on-arrival: news_headline = "Nowa Solidarność disappears after one week"

= 22 June 2023 — A challenger disappears

Spaliński resigns as secretary-general, withdraws from the party and apologises
for joining it. He disowns Szpilski over the chair's business connections and
past claim that Crimea is Russian. Kozłowski's account disappears; then so do
the accounts of Szpilski and Nowa Solidarność itself.

Whatever may remain in the party register, the functioning challenger is over.
<span class="party party-nowa-solidarnosc">**Nowa Solidarność**</span> has
achieved solidarity for seven days.

