Every one of our deputies votes against, and the statement is about the
instrument rather than the man: parliaments pass laws and budgets, they do not
issue findings of fact about the dead, and a chamber that starts doing it will
not stop at popes.

It is the correct constitutional argument and it will be edited into a
fifteen-second clip of the Left refusing to defend John Paul II. Our candidates
in the eastern counties are told to expect it at every meeting until October,
because they will.

