Our councillors and organisers do the unglamorous thing: a shared model for
ordering, storing, weighing and prioritising — pensioners and households with
small children first — circulated to every commune that will take it,
including the ones run by PiS.

People get coal. The government announces the scheme's success. In four
hundred communes the people who made it work are ours, and they are still
there at the local elections, which is a slower and better return than a week
of headlines.

