Cars in a line at four in the morning, a woman with a wheelbarrow, an empty
yard. Seven years of announcements about sovereignty and energy security end
in a photograph anybody can understand, and we make sure everybody sees it.

The photograph does not warm anybody. The communes still have to run the
scheme, they get no model from us, and a fair number of the people in that
queue conclude not that the government failed but that the entire political
class is useless — a conclusion with an address, and it is not ours.

