= April 2023 — Four months in a forest

A horse rider finds wreckage in woodland near Bydgoszcz. It is an air-launched
Russian cruise missile, and it has been lying there since December — roughly
four months, fifteen kilometres from a city of three hundred thousand people
and near a military airfield.

The air force knew something had entered the airspace in December. The search
was called off. The defence minister says he was not informed; the operational
command says it reported through the correct channel; the interior ministry
says it was a military matter. Each statement is defensible and they cannot all
be true.

There is no version of this in which the country is well served. Either the
detection failed, or the reporting failed, or the political level was told and
decided that four months of silence was preferable to an admission.

[? if defence_command_response = "": No previous Lewica intervention exists on
military command and reporting, so we start this argument from nothing.?]
[? if opposition_infosec_committee = 1: The joint opposition committee is the
one forum where this can be pursued without becoming a party quarrel about who
loves the army more.?]
[? if security_incident_pressure >= 20: This is not the first airspace incident
of this parliament, and the public has started keeping its own count.?]

- @missile23_review
- @missile23_blame
- @missile23_civil

@missile23_review
title: Demand one reporting standard from detection to the minister's desk
subtitle: Requires a standing joint forum to carry it. Fixes the chain instead of finding the guilty officer.
choose-if: opposition_infosec_committee = 1 or nik_referral_channel = 1
unavailable-subtitle: Without a joint security forum or an audit channel, a reporting-standard demand from one caucus is a press release the ministry will not answer.
